Add `operationId`s to apps/api/docs/prototype/swagger.yaml, and fix
Redocly's trailing-slash, `$ref`-sibling and unused-component warnings

Generated on 2026-11-26, against the swagger.yaml on branch
api-footprint-prototypes at b89bd04. Apply from the repository root:

  git apply apps/api/docs/prototype/claude-exploration/swagger-operation-ids.patch

After this patch, Redocly's `recommended` rules report only the missing
security scheme, the empty `servers` list and the missing `info.license`
(left for later, by the user's choice on 2026-11-26).

1. Adds a camelCase verb-noun `operationId` to each of the 10 operations:

  GET    /children                          findChildren
  POST   /children                          createChild
  POST   /children/search                   searchChildren
  GET    /children/{ypid}                   getChild
  GET    /children/{ypid}/stages            listStages
  POST   /children/{ypid}/stages            createStage
  GET    /children/{ypid}/stages/{stageid}  getStage
  PATCH  /children/{ypid}/stages/{stageid}  updateStage
  PUT    /children/{ypid}/stages/{stageid}  completeStage
  DELETE /children/{ypid}/stages/{stageid}  cancelStage

`PUT` and `DELETE` are named for what they do in this API (an accepted
`PUT` completes a stage; `DELETE` is a soft cancel), not after the HTTP
method. `GET /children` and `POST /children/search` run the same search,
so they need distinct names: `findChildren` and `searchChildren`.

2. Removes the trailing slashes from `/children/{ypid}/` and
`/children/{ypid}/stages/` (`no-path-trailing-slash`). No `$ref` or
prose in swagger.yaml or claude-exploration/ refers to the old forms.

3. Fixes the 11 `spec-ref-siblings` warnings. In OpenAPI 3.0, properties
next to a `$ref` are ignored (OpenAPI 3.0.4, Reference Object):

  - `GET /children`: removes the leftover `in`, `schema` and
    `description` beside the `postcodeHeaderParameter` `$ref`. The shared
    parameter already defines them.
  - `POST /children`: removes the redundant `type: object` beside the
    `MinimalChild` request body and the `IdentifierArray` in the `200`
    response.
  - `GET` stage: removes `minimumItems`/`maximumItems` (not keywords;
    the schema is a single `Stage`).
  - `PATCH` stage: the `Notification` is optional (user, 2026-11-26).
    The response is now `204 No Content` when there's no notification
    and `200` with a `Notification` when there is one, both with the new
    `ETag`. The operation description is updated to match.
  - `MinimalChild.Identifier`: wraps the `$ref` in `allOf` so its
    description is kept.
  - `MinimalChild.DateOfBirth`: should be nullable (user, 2026-11-26).
    Uses the `type` + `allOf` + `nullable: true` pattern that `ypid`
    already uses. Strictly, OAS 3.0.3+ says `nullable` doesn't carry
    through `allOf`, so a strict validator may still reject null; `ypid`
    has the same issue.

4. Removes the unused `MinimalChildWithFieldNames` schema
(`no-unused-components`). Nothing has used it since 82f3ce4.

